frus:attachment.p:
Certain other complaints appear aimed at the loss of profit in trade,
                            which must include, at least in part, trade in contraband with Germany;
                            while other complaints demand the prohibition of trade in contraband,
                            which appear to refer to trade with the Allies.

row.cell:
Turkish Cabinet divided. Ministers of Marine and Finance favor France;
                            Minister of War favors Germany; Minister of Interior for neutrality.
                            Invasion of Caucasus probable.

Following for Navy Department: Italy to declare war on Austria; fleet
                            at Taranto, Abruzzi, Commander in Chief; Austrian vessel sunk;
                            French-English fleet near Corfu.

Emperor replies to President Wilson’s message: Appreciates humanitarian sentiments;
                            the war thrust upon Russia; contemplation of peace premature; expresses
                            thanks.

Crisis between Austria-Hungary and Servian: Investigation into
                            assassination; Austrian ultimatum presented to Servia; Servian reply;
                            diplomatic relations severed; war declared.

Netherland Government has placed embargo on exportation of cotton;
                            however shipments in transit to Germany are permitted. Denmark has no
                            prohibition against such, exportation, so far as Germany knows.

